        sourceType = "Garrison Inn Quests",
        stepCount = 5,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - A building/visitor unlock followed by a dungeon quest; current seasonal versions can require a group.\n\n1. Establish a level 2-or-higher Garrison and build a Lunarfall Inn (Alliance) or Frostwall Tavern (Horde) in a medium plot. Level 1 of this building is sufficient. Check the visiting quest givers each daily reset until Moroes offers Feeling A Bit Morose.\n\n2. Accept Feeling A Bit Morose before travelling. Enter Iron Docks at the marked entrance on Heroic or, where available, Mythic. Normal often lacks the quest object. If today's seasonal version scales to current level, bring an appropriate group; do not assume every old dungeon difficulty is a trivial legacy solo.\n\n3. In the courtyard where the three Iron Stars can be launched, find the archery practice area. Loot the Horribly Acidic Solution on top of the barrel/crates in the northeastern corner. Continue to the docks and defeat Skulloc.\n\n4. Return to Moroes in your own Inn/Tavern, complete the quest and learn Moroes' Famous Polish. Keep the building until turn-in. If the NPC seems missing, check upstairs, the basement and behind the Inn, then leave the Garrison and return. A question mark at the central fountain can be misleading.\n\n5. If you cannot hand in, check that both the required object and Skulloc kill are credited and that the timed object is still in your bags. Collect an expired object again on a supported difficulty. Keeping the object alone is not enough to finish the quest.",
