        sourceType = "Class Vendors",
        stepCount = 6,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Rogue-only currency acquisition with two available vendor routes.\n\n1. Use a rogue. For the original Draenor route, Pick Pocket humanoids until you receive Secretive Whistle. Use it to summon Griftah, then choose Fence your loot to exchange the pilfered trinkets for Dingy Iron Coins.\n\n2. Farm new pockets at the Tomb of Lights in Talador, entrance 58.0,65.0. Inside, use the left room with two portals and pickpocket Shadow Infiltrators/Pillagers as they run toward the friendly defenders. Let the defenders kill them so new enemies arrive. Alternatively pickpocket suitable enemies around Tanaan's Throne of Kil'jaeden. The old pre-6.2 Path of Glory farm is obsolete.\n\n3. Save 10,000 Dingy Iron Coins, summon Griftah again with Secretive Whistle and buy Barrel of Bandanas. Do not spend the currency on his optional gold quests while saving for the toy.\n\n4. For the alternative Legion route, complete Call of The Uncrowned and The Final Shadow to enter the Hall of Shadows beneath Broken Isles Dalaran. At Griftah, complete Wanna Buy a Lamp? (buy his 500-gold lamp), then Shine Bright Like a Diamond (buy his 500-gold shining kit and use it). Speak to Al'Abas for The Mysterious, Magnificent Al'Abas, In the Land of Magic and Coins of Air. Keep Lamp of Al'Abas in your bags: pickpocketed Legion trinkets then convert automatically to Coins of Air, without a Fence your loot interaction.\n\n5. For that alternative, pickpocket the paired Suramar Loyalists around 44.7,66.6 or Hatecoil naga near Azsuna's Eye of Azshara entrance, 61.2,41.1. Save 50,000 Coins of Air and buy the same barrel from Griftah in the Hall of Shadows. Loyalty Is Its Own Reward (1,000 coins) and High Fash-Djinn (the six named rare treasures) upgrade the lamp but are optional for the purchase. Carry only the current lamp. Coins of Air and Dingy Iron Coins cannot be exchanged for each other.\n\n6. Learn the barrel on your rogue. The collected toy counts for account collection achievements, while placing it still requires the appropriate class.",
